{
  "_comment": [
    "One canonical set for a Thickness the platforms expose differently.",
    "",
    "A margin is a Thickness in the C#. The web platforms expose it as a sub-object and their maps",
    "record a path -- groupTextMargin.bottom, with Blazor naming the same thing GroupTextMarginBottom.",
    "The ApiGenerator flattens it instead, into four separate Double properties, and recorded them under",
    "their flattened names, so the two halves of the product disagreed about what the canonical name is",
    "and no topic could write one term that resolved everywhere.",
    "",
    "The dotted path wins: four of the six platforms already record it, and it is what a Thickness",
    "actually is. These entries bring the rest to it -- WinUI and Uno to the flattened property, WPF to",
    "the unflattened Thickness, which has no per-edge member at all.",
    "",
    "WPF maps all four edges onto the one property on purpose. A reader there sets the whole Thickness,",
    "so every edge leads to the same place, and that is the honest answer rather than four links to",
    "members WPF does not have.",
    "",
    "The parent on its own -- `groupTextMargin` with no edge -- is deliberately absent. It is a Thickness",
    "in the C# and is on no platform's public surface, so a topic naming it is naming something no reader",
    "can set. chart-data-legend and chart-data-tooltip did exactly that.",
    "",
    "Only the families the topics actually name. badgeMargin and the rest are in the web maps already and",
    "need nothing here unless a topic starts naming them."
  ],
